  "assessment": "The frozen TeX supports the three-Lorentzian-plus-linear trXAS fit at lines 213-224 and every central parameter in the equilibrium and t=0.4 ps rows at lines 230-233. Independent execution of both structured programs at omega=527.89, 528.00, 528.45, 529.00, and 529.70 eV agrees with direct evaluation of the displayed formula to at most 1.34e-15. The resulting equilibrium values are 1.05656169082892, 1.00752698419221, 0.853012149028647, 0.622352276816965, and 1.04641638166533; the t=0.4 ps values are 1.57044429987778, 1.55835525478866, 1.40026593624175, 1.03965541710160, and 1.00999436114008. The interval 527.89-529.70 eV is a conservative interval between source-reported fitted peak centers, and the sample, temperature, geometry, pump, and polarization locators are source-supported. The card is nevertheless not yet admissible as a matched family: both claims cite exactly the same fixed conditions, so the source-reported equilibrium-versus-t=0.4 ps branch identity is absent from the structured condition sets; additionally, the known-but-unspecified convention of the parenthetical fit uncertainties is encoded as an unresolved selected source ambiguity, which mechanically prevents admission even though the executable Oracle deliberately returns only deterministic central fits. A revision must add disjoint, source-anchored equilibrium/pre-pump and t=0.4 ps conditions, attach one to each claim, and retain the unspecified uncertainty convention as provenance rather than an unresolved ambiguity about the central formula. No formula or central parameter change is requested.",
